  "text": "The problem involves a triangle and its circumcircle. We will use the properties of the triangle and the circumcircle to find the required arc lengths.\n\n1. **Identify the angles of the triangle**:\n   - Given angles: \\( \\angle BAC = 84^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle ABC = 60^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle ACB = 36^\\circ \\).\n\n2. **Identify the midpoints of the sides**:\n   - \\( D \\) is the midpoint of \\( \\overline{BC} \\).\n   - \\( E \\) is the midpoint of \\( \\overline{AC} \\).\n   - \\( F \\) is the midpoint of \\( \\overline{AB} \\).\n\n3. **Circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\)**:\n   - The circumcircle of \\( \\triangle DEF \\) intersects \\( \\overline{BD} \\), \\( \\overline{AE} \\), and \\( \\overline{AF} \\) at points \\( G, H, \\) and \\( J \\) respectively.\n\n4. **Measure the arcs**:\n   - We need to find \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} \\).\n\n5. **Calculate the arcs**:\n   - Since \\( D, E, F \\) are midpoints, the arcs \\( \\widehat{DE} \\), \\( \\widehat{EF} \\), and \\( \\widehat{FD} \\) are equal to the corresponding angles of the triangle.\n   - \\( \\widehat{DE} = \\angle BAC = 84^\\circ \\).\n   - \\( \\widehat{EF} = \\angle ABC = 60^\\circ \\).\n   - \\( \\widehat{FD} = \\angle ACB = 36^\\circ \\).\n\n6. **Sum the arcs**:\n   - \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 84^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 60^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 36^\\circ \\).\n   - \\( \\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 84^\\circ + 120^\\circ + 108^\\circ = 312^\\circ \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{312}\n\\]",
